{title: Stripped of Gold}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 18:13–16}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In Hezekiah's fourteenth year,
The Assyrian [C]king drew [F]near.
Sennac[Bb]herib at[C]tacked the [Dm]land,
He took the stron[Bb]gholds [C]in his [Dm]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From Lachish Heze[C]kiah [Dm]spoke,
"I have [Bb]sinned, my [C]sins I [F]broke."
"With[Bb]draw from me, [C]I will [Dm]pay,
What[Bb]ever you de[C]mand to[Dm]day."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Three hundred [C]talents of [Dm]silver stood,
Thirty [Bb]talents of [C]gold added [Dm]to the wood.
[Bb]He gave the [C]silver found in[Dm]side,
[Bb]The house of [C]the Lord, side by [Dm]side.
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | ×4
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]From palace [C]treasuries he [Dm]drew,
[Bb]Every [C]coin that he [Dm]knew.
The [Bb]doors of the tem[C]ple he stripped [Dm]bare,
The [Bb]gold he [C]gave him [Dm]there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]He gave the [C]doors to the king of [Dm]Assyria.
{end_of_verse}
